# Recovery-intent stubs. patch_recovery.py writes .recovery-intent-<slug>.txt when it
# cannot reconstruct a real patch, and regenerable_artifacts.REGENERABLE_PATTERNS already
# declares them machine output. They were never ignored, so 67 of them were committed to
# master — bag-of-words files carrying no work, which is exactly what landed_evidence.py
# and merge_reconciliation.py grep commit messages to detect and reject.
.recovery-intent-*.txt
